# `orderby`: DS0104 pointing at `sort by`, with a fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | orderby amount desc
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..40
  PIPELINE@0..39
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    SORT_OP@20..39
      IDENT@20..27 "orderby"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      SORT_KEY@28..39
        NAME_REF@28..34
          IDENT@28..34 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        IDENT@35..39 "desc"
  WHITESPACE@39..40 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `orderby`
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | orderby amount desc
  |                     ^^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to sort rows, use `sort by`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc
which parses without errors
